WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:01.290
- [Narrator] You might not think

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:03.870
copper is worth more than a penny,

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:08.340
but in today's global economy,
it's actually worth a lot.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:11.040
For electric vehicles, windmill farms,

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:15.270
even the power grid
itself copper is essential

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:17.880
and in short supply.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.140
- At the start of the next decade,

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:20.760
we're going to have a shortfall

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.460
of over 5 million metric tons.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:26.160
- [Narrator] Here's why the
metal has become so important,

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.900
and how a severe shortage

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.530
is threatening the global
push toward electrification.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:34.110
- Electrification
essentially means moving away

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:37.890
from relying so much on fossil
fuels for our energy needs.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.290
- [Narrator] Copper is
critical to electrification

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:42.450
because it has the highest conductivity

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.670
of any non-precious metal.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:47.730
That's important when trying
to make an electric car,

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:52.710
or windmill efficient so
electricity isn't lost in transit.

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:55.950
- So copper is actually
used in a great quantity

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:57.380
for these electric vehicles,

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:00.180
and other renewable energies much more so

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:01.440
than what you would use

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.170
in a traditional fossil fuel power plant

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:06.404
or traditional cars.

00:01:06.404 --> 00:01:08.910
- [Narrator] EVs require
an estimated four times

00:01:08.910 --> 00:01:11.940
as much copper as gas fueled cars.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:14.550
Wind and solar farms also typically need

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:18.360
about twice as much copper
as coal power plants.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:19.350
- Just to demonstrate

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:21.930
how much copper is needed
for electrification

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:23.880
by 2031 we're going to need

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:26.400
over 35 million metric tons of copper,

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.080
and supply on the other hands

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.350
is supposed to lack behind
at 30 million metric tons.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:34.680
- For decades our nation has failed

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:39.680
to meet the climate crisis
with the urgency it demands.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:42.360
- [Narrator] Kamala
Harris is talking about

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.070
the Inflation Reduction Act,

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.930
which has pumped federal funds

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:48.607
toward green energy and electrification.

00:01:48.607 --> 00:01:49.440
(audience applauding)

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:52.410
- Through the law, you
basically get tax credits,

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:53.970
and also other support

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:55.770
if you are involved in
the making of, you know,

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:57.600
wind farms, or factories

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.180
that are making solar
components and whatnot.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:03.510
And obviously since copper is
such a huge component of that,

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:06.090
it's helping the prices for that as well.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:07.830
- [Narrator] In May, copper was trading

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:10.710
at a little over $3.50 cents,

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:13.740
a dramatic increase from previous years,

00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:16.260
and those prices could continue to rise.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:20.130
Goldman Sachs estimates that
demand for green uses of copper

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:23.370
drives 7% of global consumption today,

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:25.203
up from just 4% in 2020.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:29.220
And we'll account for a whopping 47%

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:33.420
of total demand growth
between 2023 and 2040.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.430
So it's no surprise that copper

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:37.950
is the word on mining leader's lips.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:38.783
- Copper.

00:02:38.783 --> 00:02:39.960
- Exciting copper development.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:41.978
- We're choosing to prioritize copper.

00:02:41.978 --> 00:02:43.470
(bus engine growling)

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:44.940
- [Narrator] It sparked a flurry

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.950
of consolidation in the industry.

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:50.160
Glencore, BHP, Rio Tinto, and Newmont

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:53.520
have all made moves to
buy up other miners.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:54.960
- They've realized that copper

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:56.580
is going to be in such a huge need

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:57.810
over the next decade or so,

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:01.770
so they have decided to
instead go buy other miners

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:04.500
to get quick access to their deposits

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:08.250
and get them producing in
the market much faster.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:09.810
- [Narrator] But all of this consolidation

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:11.970
can't create more copper.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:15.450
To find more, companies
need to open new mines,

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:17.580
which is very expensive.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:18.540
- [Mike] What we're not going to do,

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:21.210
is simply go out and
buy a stream of copper.

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:23.040
- [Narrator] Analysts
say that copper prices

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:26.670
would need to rise to
$15,000 per metric ton

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:29.310
to attract investment in new mines.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:33.510
Today prices are around $8,000 a ton,

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:37.800
and starting a new mine can
take a prohibitively long time.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.720
Deutsche Bank estimates that projects

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.910
that start applying for permits today

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:45.480
will take around 10 years
to reach first production.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:47.430
- And that's just the permitting process,

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:49.590
that's not even getting
to the production part.

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:52.140
So just imagine how long
it would take for you

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:55.830
to get any single like mine
in the producing stage.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:58.050
- [Narrator] Plus, new and current mines

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:00.570
have also faced heightened scrutiny

00:04:00.570 --> 00:04:03.600
on environmental and social grounds.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:06.390
- There is increasing amounts
of environmental unrest,

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:09.240
social unrest with regards
to them being online,

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:12.180
especially as we've seen
recently in some countries

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.660
when they're trying to do that.

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:14.700
(reporter speaking in foreign language)

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:17.250
- [Narrator] In response
to looming shortages,

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:20.430
some companies are looking
to change their products.

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:24.000
For example, Tesla is changing
the makeup of battery packs

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.880
to cut copper usage in their EVs.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:28.650
- That means we need only about a quarter

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:32.580
as much copper in the car

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:35.730
as would be needed for a 12 volt battery.

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:38.160
- [Narrator] But these
changes may not be enough.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:41.430
Electrification is only
expected to increase,

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:44.313
and with it demand for
this non-precious metal.

00:04:45.485 --> 00:04:46.470
- And that's going to be a thing

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:48.780
that's going to define,
you know, commodity markets

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:50.040
for the rest of the decade.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:51.720
And a lot of people are also saying that

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:53.730
this right now is the next big bull run

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:54.963
in commodity markets.

